'''Ancient Egg: N202''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[Summer Break Cats (Event Gacha)|Summer Break Cats]] event. It was added in [[Version 11.7 Update|Version 11.7]]. [[True Form]] improves almost all attributes and gains [[Behemoth Slayer]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 670
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Ancient Egg: N202
|name2 = Cinnabar Egg: N202
|name3 = Armored Firefly Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cinnabar Egg: N202''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Armored Firefly Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, reverting to this form may prove useful if a cheaper, more spammable meatshield is needed in an [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] stage.

==='''True Form'''===
Armored Firefly cat is a meatshield combined with a crowd controller. They can keep their traits at bay while being able to tank some hits should the frontline be breached. However, they are very reliant on their weaken to be an effective meatshield. If he can't weaken enemy due to range issues (such as [[Crustaceous Scissorex]]), you should rely on something else. Against [[Casaurian Ahirujo]], Firefly is one of the few ways to somewhat reliably crowd-control them. However, this was made redundant by [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Val Val Cat]]. While Armored Firefly isn't completely useless, one should definitely prioritize evolving much more useful eggs such as Courier Cat and [[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]] before Firefly.

